---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const APP = "https://login.ollastack.com";

const sections = [
  { id: "overview", title: "Overview" },
  { id: "create", title: "Create a form" },
  { id: "submit", title: "The submit endpoint" },
  { id: "fields", title: "Fields & validation" },
  { id: "spam", title: "Spam protection" },
  { id: "notifications", title: "Notifications" },
  { id: "more", title: "Webhooks, exports & more" },
  { id: "agents", title: "Agent submissions" },
  { id: "openapi", title: "API spec" },
];

// Code as plain strings — keeps literal { } out of Astro's JSX parser.
const cCreate = `# Create a form via the API — or just click "Create form" in the dashboard.
curl -X POST https://login.ollastack.com/api/forms \\
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"name":"Contact"}'
# → data: { "id":"frm_…", "slug":"contact",
#           "endpoint":"https://login.ollastack.com/api/submit/contact", ... }`;

const cHtml = `<!-- Point any HTML form at the endpoint — no JavaScript required. -->
<form action="https://login.ollastack.com/api/submit/contact" method="POST">
  <input name="email" type="email" required>
  <textarea name="message" required></textarea>
  <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none">  <!-- honeypot: leave empty -->
  <button>Send</button>
</form>`;

const cCurl = `# JSON and application/x-www-form-urlencoded are both accepted.
curl -X POST https://login.ollastack.com/api/submit/contact \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -d '{"email":"ada@example.com","message":"hi"}'
# → 201 Created  { "success": true, "id": "sub_…", "next": null }`;

const cErr = `# Missing/invalid fields → 400, with a message per field.
{ "error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
             "message": "Invalid input",
             "fieldErrors": { "email": ["Invalid email"] } } }`;
---

<Base
  current="docs"
  title="Docs — Forms — Ollastack"
  description="Turn any HTML form into a backend: create an endpoint, submit from HTML/JSON/curl, validate fields, block spam, and fan out to email, webhooks, and integrations."
  docsName="Forms"
  docsSlug="forms"
>
  <div class="docs-shell container-wide">
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="side-eyebrow mono">/ docs / forms</div>
      <nav>
        <ul>
          {sections.map((s) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>
      <div class="side-back">
        <a href="/docs">← All docs</a>
        <a href="/docs/agents">→ Agents submit forms</a>
        <a href="/docs/agent-mail">→ Agent Mail</a>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <article class="content">
      <span class="chip mono"><span class="dot"></span>forms</span>
      <h1 class="display">Turn any form into a backend.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Create an endpoint, point an HTML <code>action=</code> at it, and every
        submission is validated, spam-filtered, stored, and fanned out to email,
        webhooks, and integrations — no server to run. This is the short version;
        the <a href="/docs">API quickstart</a> has every language and the full
        reference lives at <a href="/docs/api">/docs/api</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
      <p>
        A <strong>form</strong> is an endpoint plus a schema. You define fields
        (in the dashboard builder or via the API), you get a URL, and anything
        that <code>POST</code>s to it becomes a stored submission. Each submission
        runs the same pipeline: <strong>validate → rate-limit → spam-filter →
        store → notify</strong>. A real lead is never silently dropped — blocked
        submissions are recorded so you can see them.
      </p>

      <h2 id="create">1. Create a form</h2>
      <p>
        Click <strong>Create form</strong> in the
        <a href={`${APP}/dashboard`}>dashboard</a>, name it, and copy the endpoint
        URL — or create one over the API (tokens live in
        <a href={`${APP}/dashboard/settings`}>Settings → API tokens</a>):
      </p>
      <pre class="code">{cCreate}</pre>

      <h2 id="submit">2. The submit endpoint</h2>
      <p>
        <code>POST /api/submit/&lt;slug&gt;</code> is the only endpoint your form
        needs, and it takes <strong>no key</strong> — a plain HTML form works:
      </p>
      <pre class="code">{cHtml}</pre>
      <p>Submitting with <code>fetch</code> / <code>curl</code> is identical:</p>
      <pre class="code">{cCurl}</pre>
      <p class="muted-note">
        <code>_gotcha</code> is a honeypot — bots fill it, humans don't. Prefer a
        hosted UI? Every form gets a server-rendered page at
        <code>{APP.replace('https://','')}/f/&lt;slug&gt;</code>, and successful
        submits route to <code>/thanks/&lt;slug&gt;</code> or a redirect you set.
      </p>

      <h2 id="fields">3. Fields &amp; validation</h2>
      <p>
        Each field in the builder has a type and a required/optional flag. The
        endpoint validates the payload before saving; a bad payload comes back as
        <code>400 VALIDATION_ERROR</code> with <code>fieldErrors</code> mapping
        each field id to its messages. Hidden fields (<code>showIf</code>
        conditional logic on Starter+) are neither validated nor stored.
      </p>
      <pre class="code">{cErr}</pre>

      <h2 id="spam">4. Spam protection (built in)</h2>
      <p>
        Every submission runs a layered filter — honeypot, IP blocklist,
        keyword/regex, link heuristics, Akismet, and a local ML classifier.
        Optional <strong>CAPTCHA</strong> (per-form <code>captchaRequired</code>)
        adds a challenge for browser submits. The rule that matters:
        <strong>a real lead is never lost</strong> — a "maybe spam" ML hit is
        <em>quarantined</em> (still delivered, just flagged), and the filter
        <strong>fails open</strong>. Blocked attempts are logged for the owner to
        review.
      </p>

      <h2 id="notifications">5. Notifications</h2>
      <p>
        Each form emails its submissions to a primary <code>notifyEmail</code>
        plus optional CC/BCC. One guardrail: every recipient must be an address
        <strong>verified on the account that owns the form</strong> — so a form
        can't be pointed at a stranger's inbox. Add an <strong>autoresponder</strong>
        to reply to the submitter automatically. To send from your own domain,
        configure <a href="/docs/smtp">custom SMTP</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="more">Webhooks, exports &amp; more</h2>
      <p>These are covered in depth on the API quickstart — the short list:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Webhooks</strong> — every non-spam submission POSTs a signed
          payload (<code>X-Ollastack-Signature</code>, HMAC-SHA256), auto-retried
          up to 5 times. <a href="/docs#webhooks">Details →</a></li>
        <li><strong>Integrations</strong> — Slack, Discord, Telegram, Mailchimp
          per form; anything else via Zapier/Make/n8n on your webhook.
          <a href="/docs/integrations">Details →</a></li>
        <li><strong>Exports</strong> — <code>GET /api/forms/&lt;id&gt;/export?format=csv</code>
          (or <code>json</code>/<code>excel</code>). <a href="/docs#exports">Details →</a></li>
        <li><strong>Analytics</strong> — daily counts, spam ratio, and geography
          per form. <a href="/docs#analytics">Details →</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="agents">Agent submissions</h2>
      <p>
        AI agents are first-class: authorize one with a Bearer token and its
        submissions are tagged with the agent's label and skip the per-IP limit
        (bots stay blocked). Full walkthrough at
        <a href="/docs/agents">/docs/agents</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="openapi">Public API spec</h2>
      <p>
        Every forms endpoint is published as OpenAPI 3.1 (public, CORS-open) so
        agents and MCP tools can discover it directly:
        <a href={`${APP}/api/openapi.json`}>{APP.replace('https://','')}/api/openapi.json</a>.
        See <a href="/docs/mcp">/docs/mcp</a> to expose it as agent tools.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={`${APP}/register`}>Create a form</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/docs">API quickstart</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .docs-shell { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; gap: 56px; padding: 64px 28px 96px; }
  .sidebar { position: sticky; top: 80px; align-self: start; }
  .side-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .sidebar nav ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
  .sidebar nav a { display: block; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .sidebar nav a:hover { background: var(--bg-sunken); color: var(--ink); }
  .side-back { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 13px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
  .side-back a { color: var(--muted); }
  .side-back a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .content { max-width: 760px; }
  .chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 3px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .chip .dot { width: 6px; height: 6px; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 50%; }
  .content h1 { font-size: 44px; margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.05; }
  .content h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 48px 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
  .content .lede { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 640px; }
  .content p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content ul { line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 22px; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content code { background: var(--bg-sunken); border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; }
  .content table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 14px 0; font-size: 14px; }
  .content th, .content td { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 10px 12px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  .content th { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-weight: 500; }
  .muted-note { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .code { background: var(--code-bg); color: var(--code-fg); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 22px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 40px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .docs-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .sidebar { position: static; } }
</style>
